  "id": "response-effect",
  "term": "response effect",
  "definition": "A response effect is a pattern in which outcomes change depending on features of an intervention, such as its type, amount, frequency, duration, or whether it is done in a group. In this source, it refers to exercise components being linked with stronger improvement in repetitive stereotyped behaviors in autism spectrum disorder.",
